## Pricing logic, compiled

A `c` unit is real C, compiled to a wasm component by our own toolchain (clang, run in-sandbox)
and executed on wasmex. `discount` takes a price and a percent and returns the marked-down price.

c :pricing do
  int discount(int price, int pct) {
    return price - (price * pct) / 100;
  }
  int render(void) { return discount(2000, 15); }
end

`show pricing` compiles the C to a wasm component, runs its `render()` on wasmex at build time,
and bakes the result (a 2000¢ item at 15% off):

show pricing

The `now` cap stamps when the sheet was priced. Just **grant** it and call it — the lane injects
the host import (a typed WIT import the Dock supplies); no boilerplate. An ungranted cap is a
hard error (`Nexus.Audit`).

c :clock, grant: [now] do
  long priced_at(void) { return now(); }
end
